Also — `this.#pushRegistration()` = `navigator.serviceWorker.ready`.

Edge: the push subscription might exist for a DIFFERENT VAPID key (if ops rotated keys) — `subscribe()` with a different applicationServerKey while already subscribed throws InvalidStateError. Handle: if getSubscription() returns existing, use it (re-POST to server to ensure server has it). Let me make #subscribe tolerant:

```js
async #subscribe() {
  const registration = await navigator.serviceWorker.ready
  const subscription = await registration.pushManager.getSubscription() || await registration.pushManager.subscribe(...)
  ...
}
```

